#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:5
#: 9b7cabd8ffe34ff480ff3737224b8a46
msgid "Battery Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:7
#: 006862149034494189b5b7bdb1528899
msgid "The battery failsafe can be configured to automatically switch the vehicle into :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>`, :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` or :ref:`Land <land-mode>` mode if the vehicle battery voltage drops below a specified voltage for 10 seconds or the estimated remaining capacity has dropped below a configurable threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:11
#: b25b350c90614c3d813561d2d88a6100
msgid "This failsafe requires the vehicle have a working :ref:`Power Module <common-powermodule-landingpage>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:13
#: 7f98d354e8114b0fb21ec4395cd250ba
msgid "ArduPilot firmware versions 4.0 and later support up to 9 batteries/power monitors. The discussion below applies to those optional batteries also. Each can trigger a failsafe and each can have different actions and setup values. In addition, a group of batteries can be treated as a single unit, see ``BATTx_MONITOR`` = 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:16
#: 9ab19053a26c45bbbc849fc9ccd7b6b5
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:18
#: 87115b8217ab47feb00c3f524c6eca77
msgid "If enabled and set-up correctly the battery failsafe will trigger if the main battery's"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:20
#: f3ad9dafa6784fc1a5d3d0b24ccffd13
msgid "voltage drops below the voltage held in the :ref:`BATT_LOW_VOLT <BATT_LOW_VOLT>` parameter (or FS_BATT_VOLTAGE in older versions) for more than 10 seconds. The default voltage is 10.5 volts. If set to zero, the voltage based trigger will be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:21
#: 83e35985f42c4b3da6f7ad271a0eb538
msgid "remaining capacity falls below the :ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>` parameter (or FS_BATT_MAH in older versions) 20% of the battery's full capacity is a good choice (i.e. \"1000\" for a 5000mAh battery). If set to zero, the capacity based trigger will be disabled (i.e. only voltage will be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:24
#: 79f442137902451aa0b338fcd2ec7ecf
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:26
#: 27515a8547fe4777b227cdd197199b46
msgid "When the failsafe is triggered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:28
#: 23ab02112cce4d8789d0bcb29a3b8cb2
msgid "Buzzer will play a loud low-battery alarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:29
#: 1dba2c6ebe124a75870a3f97b9a251ca
msgid "LEDs will flash yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:30
#: fb4111a3cbb74b59883d59aed1d7d8b2
msgid "\"Low Battery!\" will be displayed on the ground stations HUD (if telemetry is connected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:32
#: 665bae2a45bc40c08826df5b364a93a7
msgid "Then one of the following will happen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:34
#: 3a2a19b516c5422590c5c05e8c78a8aa
msgid "**Nothing** if the vehicle is already disarmed or executing RTL or Land"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:35
#: 9af998e366614186b52d1f82b68337d5
msgid "**Disarm motors** if the vehicle is in Stabilize or Acro mode and the throttle is at zero OR the vehicle is landed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:36
#: 22a79ce78e3944aeb99faeac8c619c45
msgid "The user configurable action held in the :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:38
#: d4951709536d4ed3badb3c5d8cc41d5f
msgid "**0** : Warn Only - no action will be taken"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:39
#: 5c8e370472a34172bfc4b5a3bc81b3ba
msgid "**1** : Land - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>` mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:40
#: 0d8f60ed728e453681592026c97da2a7
msgid "**2** : RTL - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Return-to-Launch <rtl-mode>` mode if possible but if not possible (because of no good position estimate) the vehicle will :ref:`Land <land-mode>` (**Recommended**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:41
#: 77528c7f610942cda91965d9127b0147
msgid "**3** : SmartRTL or RTL - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` mode if possible, if not possible (because SmartRTL's position buffer is full) the vehicle will switch to :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>`. If RTL is also not possible (because of no good position estimate) the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:42
#: 11b99f61e866491db924d2612eb6fd72
msgid "**4** : SmartRTL or Land - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` mode if possible, if not possible (because SmartRTL's position buffer is full) the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:43
#: ad299f4404b8489d8e4173b04779fd5e
msgid "**5** : Terminate - the vehicle will disarm the motors. This is a dangerous option that should not be used in most cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:44
#: d32b36d6e52845f79c8b3f8b16e52366
msgid "**6** : Auto DO_LAND_START or RTL - the vehicle will jump to the nearest \"DO_LAND_START\" mission item or RTL if no \"DO_LAND_START\" mission item has been programmed (see :ref:`common-do-land-start`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:45
#: d3f9fe2210674585b46a246fa26a58b0
msgid "**7** : Switch to :ref:`Brake mode <brake-mode>` if it can, otherwise, switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:47
#: 6de3fea1c96847df90f54c8b675ad455
msgid "As with all failsafes, the user can re-take control of the vehicle by changing the flight mode switch to another mode. The battery failsafe will not trigger again unless the two-layer failsafe is setup (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:49
#: 44812b9c901c44c28eb211551baa1a6a
msgid "The :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` parameter (Copter 4.0 and later) is a bitmask parameter to select one or more options that modify the standard actions of the radio, GCS, and battery failsafe. In the Mission Planner full parameter list or full parameter tree, the handy checkbox popup window is an easy way to set this (and any other bitmask) parameter. Be sure to go to Help > Check Beta Updates to pull the latest parameter definitions first while connected to the internet. The :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` bits are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:51
#: 56e1b623c5c240a781fda053324697cb
msgid "bit 0 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:52
#: 5f4daa3b033840c09cb4dbfcab2749ef
msgid "bit 1 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Ground Control Station Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:53
#: dfdeba9cb85d4af6ab14f577af213c02
msgid "bit 2 set: Continue if in guided mode :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:54
#: af14f084aa514f1d8b4ad2a10733b730
msgid "bit 3 set: Continue if landing on any failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:55
#: 98084076e9ca4ea2ac826138b70dde32
msgid "bit 4 set: Continue in pilot control on :ref:`Ground Control Station Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:56
#: 6e3abaf3d5174a0aa3335310cb0c70a4
msgid "bit 5 set: Release gripper during failsafe handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:57
#: 4da943f50c294d96ac99114791754bdb
msgid "if none of the above are set, then execute the :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` or :ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` options as configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:59
#: 570c9fc5cec5443bb96fe56f07682ac7
msgid "Only bitmask bit 3 & 5 affects actions taken during Battery failsafe. This parameter also works in conjunction with the GCS and radio failsafe, so ensure you are taking all options into account when setting this parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:63
#: 4bb8b324477f43149678d8c6b44a0298
msgid "Even if the failsafe action is set to \"None\" (i.e. :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 0) the buzzer will buzz and the LEDs will flash yellow. To completely disable the battery failsafe set :ref:`BATT_LOW_VOLT <BATT_LOW_VOLT>` and :ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>` to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:67
#: 3a26295463b44c5bb5c78e9fbec11237
msgid "Once the battery failsafe has triggered, it cannot be reset until the autopilot is rebooted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:70
#: 2b926afb3ff4449fb50d8b1689ea054c
msgid "Setting up using Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:72
#: 617128f820064c50bea6bcd9ae7cd601
msgid "On the **INITIAL SETUP \\| Mandatory Hardware \\| Failsafe** page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:74
#: cc81c6b4522341cb99ddf49c4d01f275
msgid "If the Battery section parameters are greyed out follow instructions to setup the :ref:`Power Module <common-powermodule-landingpage>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:75
#: 962b370df329467fa62213d78f5a4e31
msgid "Set the \"Low Battery\" threshold voltage (i.e. 10.5 volts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:76
#: 3db4dde257be45f8b99231ec43bb33aa
msgid "Set the \"Reserved MAH\" or leave as \"0\" if the failsafe should never trigger based on estimated current consumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:77
#: df39bbb6d27d40e5a2106041b1d7e08f
msgid "Select the desired behavior (Land, RTL, SmartRTL, etc) from the drop-down list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:83
#: 06bff69344e2450ab57bd736feafc01d
msgid "Two-Layer failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:85
#: 572676b586764db69517879cf8b2ac26
msgid "ArduPilot includes a two-layer battery failsafe. This allows setting up a follow-up action if the battery voltage or remaining capacity falls below an even lower threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:87
#: a0c28c94842f428c91dffd57c59d15aa
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_VOLT <BATT_CRT_VOLT>` - holds the secondary (lower) voltage threshold. Set to zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:88
#: b263b6ea5322462d93ebaa3cbf8798b7
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_MAH <BATT_CRT_MAH>` - holds the secondary (lower) capacity threshold. Set to zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:89
#: bff4e0652d0a4a948dc9bd6b330901a8
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` - holds the secondary action to take. A reasonable setup would be to have :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 2 (RTL) and :ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` = 1 (Land)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:92
#: dab4df6ef7bf4501997205d6a8f0ad65
msgid "Advanced Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:94
#: d4f26eb0eb44436091946651ebb7669f
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_VOLTSRC <BATT_FS_VOLTSRC>` allows configuring whether the raw battery voltage or a sag corrected voltage is used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:95
#: ba4a6b4aa1c64d57acfa71859241316b
msgid ":ref:`BATT_LOW_TIMER <BATT_LOW_TIMER>` can configure how long the voltage must be below the threshold for the failsafe to trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:96
#: a7122f1123e34c7d911931d82f553b5e
msgid "``BATTx_`` parameters can be setup to trigger the failsafe on other batteries"
msgstr ""
